# Benchmark outputs / caches
#
# Nothing under runs/ is tracked — it is local run state, and none of it is the published unit:
#   runs/*/cells/        ~44k tiny per-cell JSONs, one per (model, variant, dataset, split,
#                        protocol generation); they made the repo hostile to clone
#   runs/*/datasets/     raw fetched data — several sources are fetch-only /
#                        non-redistributable (the benchmark never re-hosts data)
#   runs/*/predictions/  per-row dumps, which include target values (i.e. data rows)
#   hpo_evaluations.json, trajectories.json, elo_chart.png — regenerated every run
#
# The canonical, publishable form is `results/leaderboard_cells.csv`: ONE row per
# (model, variant, dataset, split_id), written by `scripts/elo_ladder.py --export` via
# `insurarena.results.canonical`, alongside `results/elo_ladder.csv` and `results/elo_chart.png`.
# The caches stay on disk locally for replay.
/runs/
*.parquet
*.npz
results.csv

# Campaign scratch: driver logs, batteries, quarantined caches — kept on disk, out of git
/scratchpad/
/*.log
/*.pid
catboost_info/
# local secrets (API tokens)
.env
